user: When starting the `agent-runner` it seems to load the AI model. That's not nice, since that delays the launch of the application by a lot. There is also the issue of switching models. In case a different model had been in use the application will fail to launch at all. Because the timeout will hit. It is too low for the switch to occur. This also hits when the user, inside the application switched model and then tries to use it. The application will then exit, due to the timeout hitting, since the switch takes too long, before it is able to provide output. Therefore the `agent-runner` needs to learn that switching model, takes time, which means that it has to wait for that to complete before it issues any requests to the new model with the current timeout applied only to the request itself and not the switch. We'd also like to decouple the startup from loading the model, so that we quicker gets into the agent-runner without waiting for the model to load, or respond. Please fix. Thanks

