Author: Stefan Lindblad <stefan.lindblad@linux.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 09:12:56 2026 +0000

    agent-runner: make advisory language detection gitignore-aware
    
    detect_project_languages reads the project root's top-level entries and
    excludes any the project's .gitignore declares as not part of itself,
    so dev-only tooling (e.g. an installed editor CLI like Gemini's
    node_modules/package.json/package-lock.json) no longer makes the runner
    report a language the project does not use.
    
    This keeps 'what the project uses' honest. The capability gate
    (resolve_profiles + HostProbe) stays manifest-free and gitignore-blind,
    judging availability purely on whether an interpreter reaches the
    sandbox's mounted read-only roots, and remains the sole authority for
    advertising. Falls back to a raw manifest scan when no .gitignore is
    readable so a missing ignore file never hides a real language.

