    The "absent install" trial asserts that a pin for a not-installed toolchain
    produces a version-specific, actionable error mentioning both the host and the
    pinned version. That error is only emitted once an installed host rustup at
    /usr/bin/rustup has been queried and reports the channel as missing.
    
    CI installs Rust via dtolnay/rust-toolchain into the toolcache, so /usr/bin/
    rustup is absent and resolve() failed there with a "No such file or directory"
    message that never mentions the pinned version, failing the assertion. The
    trial now gates on /usr/bin/rustup being present and skips cleanly otherwise,
    so it runs in a rustup-equipped environment and does not fail in toolcache CI.

